{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>You hearken to my voice, I advise you.</b> I shall give you counsel:" "Know that the word Elohim is an epithet, as I have explained. Only because it is spoken frequently, they consider this epithet as if it were a proper noun — \"Elohim will let me gaze upon my enemies\" (Psalms 59:11); \"In the beginning Elohim created\" (Genesis 1:1) — and many like this. Therefore our Sages, of blessed memory, counted it among the names that may not be erased." "<b>And the sense of \"may Elohim be with you.\"</b> That HaShem will help you if you do thus. And he said to him at the end of the matter that he should take permission from HaShem for this counsel, and this is his saying \"and Elohim command you.\" And there is no doubt that he did so." "<b>And the sense of \"be you for the people.\"</b> On behalf of the people." "<b>Before Elohim.</b> On the part of HaShem." "<b>And you shall bring the matters.</b> If they are difficult. And these matters are those that Moses said at first, \"when they have a matter they come to me\" (Exodus 18:16). And the explanation of this follows: \"the difficult matter they shall bring to you.\""], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:35:41.730985463Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}